    skos:definition "a native sesqui-carbonate of soda, of which two kinds are obtained in Egypt, the white and the sulfate. It is employed in the manufacture of soap and glass, for bleaching and other purposes. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 269]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_natron" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Natron"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:1343 (Alkali of other Sorts Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 269, Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)."@en ;
    <ontology/attestationBasis/#resource> "document_attested" ;
